1. Project Overview
This project implements an Autonomous Research Agent using the LangChain framework and Groq’s LLaMA-3.3-70B model. The agent is designed to perform end-to-end research on any given topic by autonomously browsing the web, extracting key insights from Wikipedia, and synthesizing the findings into a formal, structured professional report.

Unlike a standard chatbot, this system uses ReAct (Reasoning and Acting) logic to determine which tool to use at each step to ensure the data is grounded in real-time information.

